      "text": "- To find the integer \\( x \\) such that when it is divided by 15, the remainder is 7, we can express this relationship as:\n    \\[\n    x \\equiv 7 \\pmod{15}\n    \\]\n- This means \\( x \\) can be written in the form:\n    \\[\n    x = 15k + 7\n    \\]\n    where \\( k \\) is an integer.\n- We want to find the remainders when \\( x \\) is divided by 3 and by 5.\n\n1. **Finding the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 3:**\n    - Consider \\( x \\equiv 7 \\pmod{15} \\)\n    - The congruence \\( x \\equiv 7 \\pmod{15} \\) implies \\( x = 15k + 7 \\).\n    - To find \\( x \\mod 3 \\), note that:\n      \\[\n      15 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{3} \\implies x = 15k + 7 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{3}\n      \\]\n    - Since \\( 7 \\mod 3 \\) equals 1, we have:\n      \\[\n      x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3}\n      \\]\n\n2. **Finding the remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 5:**\n    - Consider \\( x \\equiv 7 \\pmod{15} \\)\n    - The congruence \\( x \\equiv 7 \\pmod{15} \\) implies \\( x = 15k + 7 \\).\n    - To find \\( x \\mod 5 \\), note that:\n      \\[\n      15 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{5} \\implies x = 15k + 7 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{5}\n      \\]\n    - Since \\( 7 \\mod 5 \\) equals 2, we have:\n      \\[\n      x \\equiv 2 \\pmod{5}\n      \\]\n\n3. **Summing the remainders:**\n    - The remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 3 is 1.\n    - The remainder when \\( x \\) is divided by 5 is 2.\n    - Therefore, the sum of these remainders is:\n      \\[\n      1 + 2 = 3\n      \\]\n\nConclusion: The sum of the remainders is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).\n\nLet's verify this using Python.\n\n```python\n# Given that the integer x, when divided by 15, gives a remainder of 7\n# We need to find the remainders when x is divided by 3 and by 5\n\n# Let's assume x = 15k + 7 where k is an integer\n# Now we will find x modulo 3 and modulo 5\n\n# First, set k such that the remainder when x is divided by 3 is checked\n# Let k = 1, then x = 15*1 + 7 = 22, and we check 22 % 3\nk = 1\nx = 15 * k + 7\nremainder_3 = x % 3\nremainder_5 = x % 5\n\n# Sum of the remainders\ntotal_remainder = remainder_3 + remainder_5\nprint((x, remainder_3, remainder_5, total_remainder))\n```",
